  "tail": "Completed the assigned batch-11 items and A/B pages. The general two-stage variance proof includes the finite-fiber verification for the conditional-variance formula; the B page includes the exact village-and-field enumeration and unequal-size counterexample.\n\n- [A page](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/cluster-and-two-stage-sampling.md>) · [B page](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/library/statistical-models-and-experiments/cluster-and-two-stage-sampling-examples.md>)\n- [Batch notes](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-11.notes.md>) · [coverage](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-11.coverage.json>) · [proof contracts](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-11.proof-contracts.json>) · [cross-batch dependencies](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-11.cross-batch-dependencies.json>)\n\n**Checks:** 4/4 sources verified; 23 harvested results passed coverage review; proof contracts passed for 7/7 items; precheck passed for all 5 proof-bearing items; proof layout passed with 22 steps and 0 defects. Scoped dependency, content-policy, rendering, and manifest checks passed.\n\n**Readiness:** All seven Step-1 records are `escalated` with `owner: false`. Batch 8’s required `def-finite-population-and-sampling-design` record remains escalated and its cross-batch review remains open, despite the referenced fixed-design supplier now being owner-ready. The supplier body and proof were inspected; this pair does not claim upstream resolution or acceptance.\n\nThe run-wide dependency check could not parse the unrelated [batch-42 manifest](</home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/statistical-models-experiments-62-batch-42.pages